   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021 relating to the provision of\nrecords upon the receipt of a complaint of an incident of abuse or neglect of\nan individual with a disability, as proposed in legislative bills numbers A.\n7731 and S. 7024, in relation to the provision of such records",
    "basePrintNo": "S7847",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7847-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1 & 2, Chap of 2021 (as proposed in A.7731 & S.7024)",
    "lawSection": "Executive",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7847\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021 relating to the provision\nof records upon the receipt of a complaint of an incident of abuse or\nneglect of an individual with a disability, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers A. 7731 and S. 7024, in relation to the provision of such\nrecords\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.\n2021, c. 755, to clarify provisions relating to requirements that a\nfacility must follow when submitting records upon the receipt of a\ncomplaint of an incident of abuse or neglect of an individual with a\ndisability\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by clarifying that if the\nindependent agency's access is denied or delayed beyond the allotted\ntime frame, the facility must provide the independent agency with a\nwritten statement within one business day after the expiration of the\ndeadline with reasons for the denial or delay. This legislation adds\nthat where records are maintained electronically, they will be provided\nto the independent agency via electronic means.  Additionally, the\neffective date is 30 days after it becomes law.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 118 of 2021, this legislation is a negotiated\nchange to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 755 of the Laws of 2021. S.7024 and A.7731\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately; provided,\nhowever, that section one of this act shall take effect on the same date\nand in the same manner as a chapter of the laws of 2021 relating to the\nprovision of records upon the receipt of a complaint of an incident of\nabuse or neglect of an individual with a disability, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers A.7731 and S.7024, takes effect.\n",
